      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You have perfectly identified the core vulnerability of absolute \"security\" claims: without clear, independent criteria and strict procedural checks, the power to define an \"emergency\" inevitably becomes a tool for authoritarian control. This is why international human rights standards insist that any such restrictions must be narrowly tailored, publicly justified, and subject to judicial review to prevent them from becoming a permanent loophole. Ultimately, the distinction isn't in the existence of the power to restrict, but in the rigid legal safeguards that prevent that power from being used to suppress legitimate political dissent under the guise of safety.",
      "source": "target",
